<title>GERMANY: Fresenius plans takeover of Italian SIFRA.</title>
<headline>Fresenius plans takeover of Italian SIFRA.</headline>
<dateline>BAD HOMBURG, Germany 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>German pharmaceuticals group Fresenius AG said on Thursday that it would take over the Italian infusion firm SIFRA S.p.A., following the approval of the relevant cartel authorities.</p>
<p>The takeover was also subject to the approval of the supervisory board of Fresenius, the group said in a compulsory statement.</p>
<p>SIFRA had sales of around 123 million marks ($73 million) in 1996 and has a payroll of 431 employees. Around 90 percent of sales are in Italy and the company is based in Isola della Scala, near Verona, with production facilities there and in Enna in Sicily.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525 ($ = 1.686 German Marks)</p>
